\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{\code{hP} (→ D-RT-05) is an augmented virtual equipment when \code{P} is (\ref{at-ft-0008}). Riehl–Verity-style arguments — proofs in the homotopy 2-category and in the set-level equipment of modules — are carried out in \code{hP} and lifted to \code{P} by truncation lemmas where the ∞-statement is a \code{π₀}-statement. This is the cheap track: many (∞,1)-theorems (adjunctions, absolute liftings, limits as absolute liftings) are set-level statements about \code{hP}.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Coherence lives in \code{P}; the formal layer is set-level. Banking these results early is low-risk and validates \ref{dec-ft-0003} before the coherent versions are built.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{frozen at \ref{ms-0005}.}
}
